            <ArticleTitle>A case of elongated pterygoid hamulus syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>131-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Elongation of the pterygoid hamulus is a rare syndrome that shows various and complex symptoms in the palatal and pharyngeal region. A case of elongated pterygoid hamulus syndrome in a 47-year old man is reported here.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
